10 ' BUG HUNT - a first person shooter made with the software 3D sector renderer (W3D ...) of Engine1999.
20 ' A research bunker has been overrun by giant robot bugs. Fight your way from the start room through the arena, take the red key from the west
30 ' room, open the red door in the east, ride the lift up, take the blue key and leave through the blue door. Crawlers bite when they are close,
40 ' spitters stay away and shoot green globs at you. Medkits and ammo boxes lie around.
50 ' Keys: arrows or WASD walk and turn (A and D slide sideways), SHIFT runs, SPACE or CTRL fires, E or RETURN opens doors, R and F look up and down,
60 ' O opens the 3D settings (invert the X or Y axis, gamma, field of view, turning speed; they are kept for next time), M turns the music on and off, P pauses, Q or ESC quits.
70 ' Game controller: left stick walks, right stick turns and looks, A or the right trigger fires, X opens doors, LT runs, Y the settings,
80 ' START pauses, BACK quits.
90 ' How it is made: the level is DATA (rectangular sectors with floor and ceiling heights, light, tags and walls, some of them portals), read into
100 ' W3D SECTOR / W3D WALL. Doors and the lift are sectors whose heights change (W3D HEIGHT). The bugs, pick-ups, globs and decorations are things
110 ' (W3D THING): a bug walks with W3D THINGMOVE (which also keeps it out of walls), notices you with W3D("SEES", n), and your shot is
120 ' W3D("SHOOT", range). The textures and sprites are drawn with GFX statements (library w3dkit) and grabbed. Window only.
130 LOAD LIBRARY "w3dkit"
140 LOAD LIBRARY "input"
150 LOAD LIBRARY "text"
160 LOAD LIBRARY "prefs3d"
170 LOAD LIBRARY "music3d":LOAD LIBRARY "banner3d":CALL B3_S3D("BUG HUNT")
180 BREAK OFF
190 ON ERROR GOTO FAILED
200 DIM MT(40),MS(40),MH(40),MC(40),ML(40),MA(40),PK(60),PT(60),PA(60),QA(16),QX(16),QY(16),QL(16),DSEC(3),DOP(3),DCUR(3)
210 GOTO MAIN
220 FUNC CI(H,S)
230   RETURN 16+H*16+S
240 END FUNC
250 FUNC RI(M)
260   RETURN INT(RND(1)*M)
270 END FUNC
